WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.330
- All righty then, it
is time for Drew's News,

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:06.529
your fresh news linguini in a creamy

00:00:06.529 --> 00:00:08.610
(slurps) good news sauce.

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:09.550
And with me at the desk

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.120
is my trusty co-pilot, Ross Matthews.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.284
- Yummy, hi everybody.

00:00:14.284 --> 00:00:17.500
Hi guys. Hi Drew.
(audience cheers)

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.320
- Okay, so first up in the news today

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.380
is a little "Keeping Up
With the Kardashians",

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:23.213
although I don't believe

00:00:23.213 --> 00:00:24.650
that's what we're calling it anymore

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:27.760
because they are back with a new show,

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.720
proving they are yet again an open book.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.130
So just last summer,

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.300
they said goodbye

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.670
to the old "Keeping Up
With the Kardashians"

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:36.940
after 20 seasons.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:38.844
That's a very round number.

00:00:38.844 --> 00:00:41.970
But now People reports that they are back

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:45.780
and bearing all the goods
on "The Kardashians",

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.530
which is their new reality series

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:50.790
coming to Hulu on April 14th,

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:52.820
and we have a trailer hot off the presses.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:53.680
Take a look.

00:00:54.694 --> 00:00:56.300
(upbeat music)

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.600
- [Kim] Over the last year

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:01.723
we have seen such
transformations in all of us.

00:01:02.764 --> 00:01:04.210
- Yes.
- Yes.

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:05.393
- This is day one.

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:08.960
- Okay.
(audience cheering)

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:10.390
Yeah, I know.
(audience applauding)

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:11.990
I mean-

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:12.840
- Ross.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.472
- Yes?

00:01:14.472 --> 00:01:15.470
- You gonna watch?

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:16.810
- Uh, you think?

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.860
Yeah, I'm gonna, are you all gonna watch?

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:21.400
Hello, I wanna know.
(audience cheering)

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:24.640
You know what's so interesting
about their show always

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.700
is we know kind of in the headlines,

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.000
the pop culture headlines,
what's going on with them.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.250
But then when the show
airs we get to go deep

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:34.110
and think about what's been
going on lately with them.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:37.000
I mean, Kim hosted SNL,
then the Pete Davidson,

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.770
then the Kanye of it all,
then the Tristan of it all,

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:42.590
then Kylie with the baby and
the Courtney and the Travis.

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:46.410
Hello, I want all the deets
and they're gonna serve it up,

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:47.770
I know they will.

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:50.460
- I never watched the original show

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:54.093
'cause I'm not the biggest
reality TV person as you know.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.730
But I feel like if you
didn't watch the show,

00:01:57.730 --> 00:01:59.453
and I've always followed that.

00:02:00.564 --> 00:02:02.730
I'm right up with,

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:05.260
I do keep up up with the Kardashians.

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:08.270
And you don't have to
watch the television show

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:11.350
to be an aficionado of them
because they're everywhere.

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:13.850
But I feel like this one I could jump into

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:15.640
because we're kind of up to date

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:20.370
and there's so much going
on and maybe it's a 2.0.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:23.920
- It is 2.0 and it's
not like the "Godfather"

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:25.580
where you have to have
watched the first one

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:26.740
to get the second one.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:28.347
You don't have to have to have watched

00:02:28.347 --> 00:02:30.610
"Keeping Up With the
Kardashians" to get this one.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:31.443
You can just jump in-

00:02:31.443 --> 00:02:33.720
- Which I am one of those
psychological persons

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.040
where I'm like oh, there's
19 years I gotta catch up on.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:36.873
Forget it.

00:02:36.873 --> 00:02:38.890
This one is a fresh
start, so I think I'm in.

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:39.723
- I'm in too.

00:02:39.723 --> 00:02:41.190
All right, we'll be
watching that coming up.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:43.920
All right, next up we've got
a man from New Jersey Shore

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.800
who got a shocking seafood surprise.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:47.633
Listen to this.

00:02:47.633 --> 00:02:50.000
The New York Post reports
Michael and Maria Spressler

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.020
were out at their favorite
restaurant in Cape May

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:53.460
called The Lobster House

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:57.270
when Michael ordered his
usual clam appetizer, delish.

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:59.630
Except this time on the 12th clam

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:03.390
he bit down on something really hard.

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:04.897
And as you can imagine, Michael thought,

00:03:04.897 --> 00:03:06.270
"Oh no, I lost a tooth."

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:09.903
But when he spit it out it was a pearl.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:11.950
A pearl.

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:14.570
It turns out the 8.8 millimeter pearl

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:18.170
could be worth thousands of dollars.

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:20.840
Now that's what we call
winner, winner clam dinner.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.110
The only thing a clam
ever gave me was diarrhea.

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:24.735
Thanks so much.

00:03:24.735 --> 00:03:28.540
He gets a pearl, that is
winning the appetizer lottery.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.490
- I know, I love,

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:32.310
thank God he didn't swallow it.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:33.720
- I know, can you imagine?

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.764
Even if I swallowed it I'd
still be getting it back.

00:03:35.764 --> 00:03:38.310
(audience laughing)

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:39.960
I don't wanna go into details but

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.640
they're deciding if Michael's
wife is gonna make it

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:44.140
into a piece of jewelry,

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:46.617
and he was like "Well,
let's get it appraised first

00:03:46.617 --> 00:03:47.450
"before we do that."

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:51.003
- Oh, I say sell and collect the clams!

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:56.007
- Hey! Yes, I'm (indistinct) you.

00:03:57.014 --> 00:03:59.597
(upbeat music)

